  - projection and aperture boundaries
  - adaptive inquiry selection and replay receipts
  - open relation ports and return-to-open foreground state
  - typed Relation Addresses behind slash paths
  - relational Observation with observer/observed role separation

receives:
  - readme.yawn
  - shape primitives
  - scientific frame
  - bridge-layer core files

produces:
  - public ontology terms
  - safe movement rules
  - reusable mental models

questions:
  - what is the smallest true concept here
  - how does movement stay bounded
  - what does proof protect
  - what arena is the smallest adequate cut
  - when should a signal attach, nest, link, merge, split, or remain held
  - when should an objective receive its own Yawn and sleeping bot
  - which orientation question or explicit hold is useful now
  - which typed relation does a slash path project, and is it genuine parentage
  - when may an engaged relationship return to an open foreground without deleting history

